-- ============================================================================
-- DR8 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Completion Design, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). Structure row generated from the tier's manifest.json.
--
-- What this tier owns: the completion moves. Four effects change the length of
-- a tubing string and this course computes NONE of them; it takes a length
-- change as an input from Casing and Tubing Design and asks a purely geometric
-- question about where to land a seal assembly in a polished bore.
--
-- THE CENTRAL RESULT, AND IT IS AN IDENTITY. Available travel upward plus
-- available travel downward equals the receptacle length at EVERY insertion
-- depth. Elongation pushes the seals deeper and consumes the bore below them;
-- contraction pulls them out and consumes the insertion depth itself. So the
-- landing splits a FIXED budget at an exchange rate of exactly one, which rules
-- out solving the two directions independently and rules out the idea that a
-- deeper landing is simply safer.
--
-- THE PUBLISHED JOB LANDS OUTSIDE ITS OWN BAND. A 6.1 m bore against an
-- elongation of 1.2 m and a contraction of 2.8, at a margin of 0.5, has a band
-- of acceptable landings from 3.3 to 4.4 m, width 1.1, middle 3.85. The
-- published landing is 3.0 m, which is 0.3 m SHALLOWER than the lower edge, and
-- that 0.3 m is exactly the amount by which the contraction case's remaining
-- travel of 0.2 m falls short of the 0.5 m margin. The two are the same fact
-- seen from two sides. The job is not a failure: it works, and it does not
-- deliver the margin the design stated for itself. The midpoint of the bore at
-- 3.05 m is ALSO outside the band, which is what disposes of the rule of thumb.
--
-- THE SIZING RESULT, DERIVED TWICE. The shortest usable bore is the whole swing
-- plus twice the margin, once from setting the band width to zero and once from
-- requiring the seals to stay inside at both extremes with a margin. For the
-- published cases that is 5.0 m against a 6.1 m bore, and the 1.1 m surplus IS
-- the band width: every metre of bore beyond the minimum buys exactly one metre
-- of tolerance on where the seals land.
--
-- THE JOIN WITH DR6, WHICH NEITHER COURSE COULD MAKE ALONE. Casing and Tubing
-- Design ended on three tubing cases with length changes of 0.894760459,
-- -1.810479082 and -3.345136113 m, and found that two of the three stroked out
-- of a 1.5 m seal stroke. This tier takes the same three numbers: the swing is
-- 4.239896572 m, the shortest usable bore 5.239896572, and in the published
-- 6.1 m bore the band runs 3.845136113 to 4.705239540999999 with a middle at
-- 4.275187827. Landed there, all three cases PASS. Neither conclusion
-- contradicts the other; they answer different questions and compose.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored engine; the
-- teaching lab is pinned by completionLab.test.js. Numeric and leakage sweeps
-- over the lessons and the banks are clean.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

